# Chrome type & row proportion

When adding or restyling **filter lists, command palettes, menus, pickers**,
or similar dense chrome lists in this repo:

## Do

1. **Name the primary row model** from a product reference before writing CSS:
   - **Single-line** (Cursor Actions): icon centered on the row; ~32–36dp;
     optional `description` is not the default.
   - **Two-line**: icon/shortcut align to the **title line only**; label↔description
     gap ≥ `--fynns-space-2xs`.
2. **Type ladder — one t-shirt step max** in one panel (`sm`↔`xs` or `md`↔`sm`).
   Command chrome: label/search → `font-size-sm`; group/description/shortcut →
   `font-size-xs`.
3. **Breath from item `padding-block`**, not from crushing text gaps or inventing
   a second type scale.
4. **Split shortcut strings** into separate key chips (`Ctrl` `K`), not one blob.
5. **Measure** (font-size, icon mid vs label mid) against the reference before
   calling UI done — see browser-verify-ui.

## Don't

- Label at `md` (16) beside group captions at `xs` (12)
- `gap: 0` between title and description under a large title (“行间距崩溃”)
- Assume “icons never center” or “always center” — **follow the row model**
- Copy a two-line layout when the approved screenshot is single-line (or reverse)

